  "body": "Stacked on #1418 (merge it first). Its diff here includes #1418's commits until it merges; #1418 currently conflicts with main (not fixed here).\n\n## What changed\n- `.github/workflows/post-merge.yml`: push to `main` + `workflow_dispatch` (input `ref`); `[self-hosted, linux]`; concurrency `post-merge-main`, cancel-in-progress; `cargo xtask gate batch` under `xvfb-run -a`; gate-logs + gate-output always uploaded; no token on disk during tests.\n- Sharing with the cut: skips itself (green, notice) when a `cut.yml` run is queued/in progress or a same-repo `release/v*` PR is open (`.github/scripts/post-merge-skip.sh`). Chosen as the simplest rule that cannot starve a cut; the cut's release gate covers main then.\n- Reporting (`.github/scripts/post-merge-report.sh`, report job only, `issues: write`): one rolling issue `main is red (post-merge gate)`; red opens it (P1, source:agent, effort:low, area:build) or comments on the open one; green comments the sha and closes it. P0 when a failing step name matches golden|gcode|g_code|post (heuristic on binary names; follow-up: a real \"posted output\" tag).\n- AGENTS.md: \"Fixes are tested in the background\" (workflow first, local batch is the fallback), \"GitHub Actions minutes are budgeted\" (push to main allowed for self-hosted only, quoting the user), cut-runner section note. PROCESS_VERSION 61 (upstream is 60; #1418 also bumps, settled at merge). Decision: `docs/decisions/1451-post-merge-gate.md`.\n\n## Tested\nactionlint clean on post-merge.yml and cut.yml; YAML parses; `cargo xtask gate batch --dry-run`; both scripts run locally against a fake `gh` (idle / cut running / release PR open; red new, red existing with P0 escalation, green close, green no issue).\n\n## Not exercised\nThe workflow itself (needs the runner and a merge to main), real `gh` search for the issue title, the artifact download in the report job. xtask untouched.\n\nNeeds-maintainer: `.github` change. Changelog: none\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1451\n",
